Vikram and Betal: The Careful Planner (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100150

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a boy who always planned his work carefully,” said Betal. “He never rushed into things.”

One day, his friends started building a small bridge across a stream.

They began quickly without thinking.

But their bridge broke.

The boy took his time.

He measured the distance and used strong materials.

He built the bridge step by step.

Soon, his bridge stood firm.

Everyone used his bridge safely.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what made the boy successful?”

Vikram replied, “Careful planning and patience made him successful.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Planning and patience lead to success.
